---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, buildBreadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | pictojxl.com';
const description =
  'Privacy Policy for pictojxl.com — client-side JPEG XL conversion. Images never leave your device. Learn how cookies, ads, and analytics are handled.';

const jsonLd = [
  buildBreadcrumbLd([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy-policy' },
  ]),
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy-policy" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <LegalPage
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="How pictojxl.com handles privacy, cookies, advertising, and analytics."
  >
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Webwise Private Company Ltd</strong> (“Webwise,”
      “we,” “us,” or “our”), a company based in the United States, operates the website
      <a href={absoluteUrl('/')}>pictojxl.com</a> (the “Service”). By using the Service, you agree
      to this Policy.
    </p>

    <h2>1. The Client-Side Privacy Guarantee</h2>
    <p>
      All image conversions and processing take place locally on your device using WebAssembly
      technology. Your files, photos, and converted images are <strong>never</strong> uploaded to,
      stored on, or transmitted to our servers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Encoding and decoding run in your browser (including Web Workers where available). We do not
      operate a cloud conversion pipeline for your images, and we do not claim ownership of any
      content you process with the tool.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <h3>2.1 Information you provide</h3>
    <p>
      If you contact us by email (for example at
      <a href="mailto:support@pictojxl.com">support@pictojxl.com</a>), we receive the information
      you include in that message (such as your email address and message content) so we can
      respond.
    </p>
    <h3>2.2 Technical and usage data</h3>
    <p>
      Like most websites, our hosting and security layers may process standard technical data such
      as IP address, browser type, device type, operating system, referring URLs, and approximate
      timestamps. This data is used to operate, secure, and improve the Service—not to reconstruct
      your images.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Google AdSense &amp; Advertising Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We may use Google AdSense and related Google advertising services to display ads on the
      Service. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user’s
      prior visits to your website or other websites.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on visits
      to this site and/or other sites on the Internet. Users may opt out of personalized
      advertising by visiting
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
        >Google Ads Settings</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      For more information about how Google uses data when you use our sites or apps, see
      <a
        href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Analytics and Log Data</h2>
    <p>
      We may use analytics tools (such as Google Analytics or privacy-focused alternatives) to
      understand aggregate traffic and performance. These tools may collect non-personally
      identifying technical information such as browser type, operating system, general geographic
      region, and anonymized or aggregated usage metrics. Where available, IP anonymization features
      may be enabled. Analytics data is used to maintain site reliability and improve user
      experience—not to identify the contents of your image files.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
    <p>
      We and our partners may use cookies and similar technologies for essential site functions and
      advertising. See our <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for details on categories of
      cookies and how to manage them.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Children’s Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service does not knowingly collect any personal information from children under the age of
      13. If you believe a child has provided us personal information through a contact channel,
      please email <a href="mailto:support@pictojxl.com">support@pictojxl.com</a> and we will take
      appropriate steps to delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Because image conversion is performed on your device, we do not retain your image files on our
      servers. Contact emails and standard server/security logs are retained only as long as needed
      for support, security, legal compliance, and legitimate business operations.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>
      The Service may link to third-party sites (for example Google policies or ads settings). We
      are not responsible for the privacy practices of those sites.
    </p>

    <h2>9. International Users</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is operated by Webwise Private Company Ltd in the United States. If you access
      the Service from other regions, you understand that technical processing related to site
      delivery may occur in the U.S. or other locations where our providers operate. Your image
      conversion itself remains local to your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top of
      this page will change when we do. Continued use of the Service after updates constitutes
      acceptance of the revised Policy.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this Privacy Policy?<br />
      Webwise Private Company Ltd (USA)<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:support@pictojxl.com">support@pictojxl.com</a><br />
      Website: <a href={absoluteUrl('/')}>https://pictojxl.com</a>
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
